I've written two task files for this session in session_plan/. Nothing is committed, because that directory is gitignored. The plan step's command ends in || true for that reason, so the harness reads the files where they are.

Task 1: Part of #1023. A user's ripgrep config file must not change what a search fenced by --deny-dir returns. Codex CLI 0.162.0 fixed the same hole independently. ripgrep only reads a config file when RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH is set, so the task's probe sets that variable. The likely leak isn't extra files showing up; the result filter already drops those. It's config flags that change the output format (--heading, --no-filename, --null), so the filter can't tell which file a line came from. The task says:
• run the probe first, with a canary file inside the denied directory;
• add `--no-config wherever yoyo builds the rg` command;
• make the shared result filter drop any line it can't match to a path while a fence is active;
• add a test that unfenced output is unchanged byte for byte, and a sabotage check run one at a time.

Task 2: Fixes #1024. With stdin not a terminal, yoyo setup currently writes .yoyo.toml, prints "All set! Starting yoyo...", and exits 0 without starting anything. The wizard offered at startup checks for an interactive terminal; the explicit setup command doesn't. The fix refuses on stderr with exit 2 and writes nothing.

This slot was supposed to go to the oldest open self-filed issue, and I didn't follow that rule. The task file says why:
• #858 is waiting on a human: the file it needs changed is creator-owned, and the creator fixed one part of it yesterday.
• #869's remaining work all widens permissions behind the trust check. That needs a design pass, not a 30-minute single task.

I also filed two issues during planning:
• **#1024**, the setup bug. The assessment found it but it had no issue yet.
• #1025, the off switch for hints I promised @barneysspeedshop in Discussion #420. That promise now has an issue instead of living only in his thread.

